},{"finding_id":"circuit/f6-can1-no-protection","disposition":"noted","reason":"Verified in connectivity: '/CAN+' [J1.47,J2.93] and '/CAN-' [J1.46,J2.94] contain only the harness and module connector pins, with no TVS, filter, or termination footprints, in contrast to CAN2 which carries D10/D11 (NUP2105L), 47p filters, and terminator footprints. No declared criterion requires base-board CAN1 protection, the CAN1 transceiver lives on the Polygonus module whose internals are explicitly out of this donor review's scope, and automotive transient qualification is a declared limitation. Supported info-level observation of the asymmetric protection scheme; canonical record for this topic.","evidence":[{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"'/CAN+':[J1.47,J2.93]; '/CAN-':[J1.46,J2.94]; contrast '/CAN2+'/'/CAN2-' containing D10/D11, C29/C30/C33/C34, R36/R37"},{"path":"inputs/project/README.md","locator":"Features/Connectivity: 'Dual CAN'; declared_limitations: modular design, transients/EMC out of scope"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-001","disposition":"duplicate","duplicate_of":"check/drc","reason":"Identical to the accepted check/drc defect: same 13 error-severity DRC violations (padstack x5, annular_width x5, starved_thermal x3) from the same tool run, known only through the tool's own summary because the individual entries fall beyond the supplied drc.json excerpt. Defect-to-defect duplication keeps it attached to the accepted canonical check finding.","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"by_type {padstack:5, annular_width:5, starved_thermal:3}; by_severity error=13"},{"path":"work/drc/console.log","locator":"'Found 142 violations'"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-002","disposition":"deferred","reason":"Major-severity concern that evidence confirms but does not resolve. The native sheet proves R36/R37 are DNP (symbol uuid d69380f9: value 120, in_bom no, dnp yes applied to both instances), connectivity and geometry confirm both terminators sit correctly at the two transceiver ends of /CAN2+-/CAN2-, and the README advertises internal wideband operation on CAN bus #2. Whether the all-DNP population is a deliberate builder option (the bus is also exposed on J1 pins 11/15, where internal termination would conflict with harness terminators) or an omission cannot be determined from the packet; no population/termination requirement is declared. Per adjudication rules a major concern cannot be merely noted, and inventing a termination requirement is not permitted, so it is deferred pending design-intent documentation or build instructions.","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol uuid d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543: Value '120', (in_bom no), (dnp yes), instances R36 (/2889b04e...) and R37 (/10870bd0...)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"R36/R37 dnp:true; '/CAN2+':[C29.2,C33.2,D10.1,D11.1,J1.15,J2.73,R36.1,R37.1,U20.7,U21.7]"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"R36 dnp:true, pads on /CAN2+ and /CAN2- at (175.01,142.13); U21 at (75.48,140.27)"},{"path":"inputs/project/README.md","locator":"'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers ... connected internally to CAN bus #2'"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-003","disposition":"duplicate","duplicate_of":"check/erc","reason":"Restates the same 5 error-severity ERC violations established by the accepted check/erc finding (same uuids ad746bdd/acdd6b6d/3d2dd476/a25f94e0/2f453565-b5fc1cf2, same locations and types). Defect-to-defect duplication preserves the defect under the accepted canonical check record.","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"root sheet '/': power_pin_not_driven x3, pin_to_pin (J2 pins 40/41), pin_not_connected (A1 pin 2 ~FLT)"},{"path":"work/erc/console.log","locator":"'Found 353 violations'"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-004","disposition":"noted","reason":"Verified parity observation: the board carries Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD for J2 while the schematic symbol assigns fome_modules:polygonus, plus a BOM-attribute mismatch (both visible in the drc.json parity section). No electrical defect is established: DRC reports 0 unconnected items and the J2 pads carry the expected nets throughout, indicating the variant footprint's pad numbering maps correctly; the substitution is plausibly an intentional USB/SWD variant. Supported minor configuration-management concern that violates no declared criterion; the mechanical compatibility caveat stands but cannot be evaluated with the Simon library absent. Canonical record for this topic.","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"schematic_parity entries for Footprint J2 uuid f447e585-df78-4239-b8cb-4653b3837bb1: footprint name mismatch and 'Exclude from bill of materials' mismatch"},{"path":"work/drc/console.log","locator":"'Found 0 unconnected items'"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"J2 pin nets populated across all functions (power, CAN, I/O)"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-005","disposition":"noted","reason":"Verified coverage limitation, not a board defect: ERC reports lib_symbol_mismatch=89, lib_symbol_issues=14, footprint_link_issues=8 and DRC reports lib_footprint_mismatch=106, lib_footprint_issues=9 because the Simon, hellen-one-common, fome_modules and related project libraries are absent from the sandbox, so cached symbols/footprints cannot be validated against sources. This weakens the effective breadth of the native rule coverage claimed in scope but violates no design criterion; the checks themselves executed. Supported minor concern, noted.","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"by_type lib_symbol_mismatch=89, lib_symbol_issues=14, footprint_link_issues=8; e.g. 'The current configuration does not include the footprint library Simon' for J1 uuid 6971898b"},{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"by_type lib_footprint_mismatch=106, lib_footprint_issues=9; e.g. 'The current configuration does not include the footprint library Simon' for J1 uuid 93ba26da"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-006","disposition":"noted","reason":"Verified: ERC reports 229 endpoint_off_grid warnings with sampled entries confirmed in the report (e.g. uuid 15d9afbe at 286.385,107.315; R25 pin 1 at 107.315,80.01; R34 pin 1 at 165.735,75.565). No present-day connectivity fault exists: the netlist resolves all affected nets with expected members and DRC reports 0 unconnected items, so no criterion is currently violated. This is a supported latent-risk hygiene concern (fragility under future edits, concentrated in the VR conditioner analog front end), correctly preserved as a non-defect observation.","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"by_type endpoint_off_grid=229; sampled uuids 15d9afbe, 34654827 (R25 pin 1), c2f74bd3 (R34 pin 1)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"Net-(R25-Pad1), Net-(U10-IN-), Net-(U10-BIAS) etc. resolve with expected members"},{"path":"work/drc/console.log","locator":"'Found 0 unconnected items'"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-007","disposition":"noted","reason":"Verified and explicitly declared: the packet's declared_limitations state the candidate adds VR Conditioner.kicad_sch as a byte copy of the lowercase original as a disposable alias, and the netlist export confirms the hierarchy resolves through it (sheet 4 source 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch', schematic_files list). Two case-differing byte-identical files are a real fork/collision risk for future edits, but this is a declared workaround of the review scaffolding, not a defect in the design under review; all verified connectivity applies to the alias as supplied. Supported minor concern, noted.","evidence":[{"path":"work/netlist/design.xml","locator":"sheet number 4 name '/VR Conditioner/' source 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"sheet '/VR Conditioner/' uuid 76f66c7e-94ea-4f9a-aa2e-a01725934e38 hosting C23-C25, R25-R34, U10, JP1"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-008","disposition":"duplicate","duplicate_of":"circuit/f6-can1-no-protection","reason":"Same observation as circuit/f6: CAN1 nets /CAN+ and /CAN- run connector-to-module with no on-board protection, filtering, or termination footprints, in contrast to CAN2. circuit/f6 is the surviving canonical noted record (it additionally cites the README's modular-architecture context); concern-to-concern duplication, no defect status lost.","evidence":[{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"'/CAN+':[J1.47,J2.93]; '/CAN-':[J1.46,J2.94] vs '/CAN2+'/'/CAN2-' with D10/D11, C29/C30/C33/C34, R36/R37"}]}]},"ttft_ms":73842,"type":"result","duration_ms":156046,"uuid":"73e84666-cb5a-43f9-b30f-1c2bd3d203fc","ttft_stream_ms":4245,"time_to_request_ms":302,"first_content_frame_ms":4245,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
